# AI Job Search - hints for Goose

This workspace is the Spanish adaptation of the **AI Job Search** framework. Its
canonical specifications live in the files below and must not be duplicated in
this file - point at them, so upstream improvements keep reaching the fork.
Always start by reading these, in this order:

1. `AGENTS.md` - the cross-runtime entry point and the thin-pointer design.
2. `CLAUDE.md` - the candidate profile and the workflow rules.
3. `.claude/` - the canonical workflow specs: `commands/` (setup, scrape, rank,
   apply, outcome, interview, upskill, ...) and `skills/`.
4. `.agents/skills/` - the job-portal search CLIs (portable Agent Skills, one
   `SKILL.md` per portal).

Goose reads this `.goosehints` file automatically, and also honours `AGENTS.md`.
When the user asks for a workflow, open the matching `.claude/commands/<name>.md`
and follow it; to load a skill, read `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Slash
commands (`/scrape`) are Claude Code artifacts - in Goose you name the spec file.

Never restate a spec from `.claude/` here; point at it instead. Platform and
runtime notes: `COMPATIBILITY.md`.
